# Docker build context — keep it to what the build actually needs.
#
# The MCP Dockerfiles bundle the takeoff engine from web/src/lib, while the
# self-hosted web Dockerfile selects web/ and its nginx config from the same
# repository-root context. Keep that shared context free of git history and
# generated local artifacts.
#
# This is not only a speed fix. A remote builder (Glama's, among others) pays
# for that context on every build, and a build that fails for being too big or
# too slow looks exactly like a build that fails for being broken.

.git
.github
.gitignore

# Installed trees — every stage runs its own `npm ci`.
**/node_modules

# Build output — regenerated in the build stage.
**/dist
mcp/*.mcpb

# Fetched at deploy time by web/scripts/fetch-voice-model.mjs (~44 MB), never
# read by the MCP server.
web/public/models

# Docs and development fixtures: neither container build reads them. Keep
# web/public/demo in the context: the self-hosted browser image serves its
# bundled sample plan at runtime.
docs
demo
web/test
web/bench
capture
server
*.md
!mcp/README.md

# Local noise.
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store
.env
.env.*
*.log
